+## Multiple repositories with one GitHub account
+
+Keep `sources.github.config.repository` as the original primary repository and add
+`additionalRepositories: [{ repository: 'owner/another-repo' }]` in the GitHub Source.
+Setup verifies push access to every repository with the same CLI. The existing source
+polls each repository; there is no additional service, queue or Worker runtime.
+Primary repository thread IDs/cursors remain unchanged. Additional repository IDs
+and cursors are repository-qualified; Worker environment, replies and PR claims use
+the originating repository. Do not reorder the primary repository to migrate history.
+
+Workers can use existing `github/issues/...` resources in their own repository;
+main-session cross-repository reads use `github/repos/owner/repo/issues/...`.
+Existing admission, self-authored Issue and mention rules still apply.
